  <p class="standfirst">TikTok prints its safe zone. Not in the text of any help page, but on the template files those pages hand out, in pixels, and almost nobody quotes them.</p>

  <h2>What are TikTok's video specs in 2026?</h2>

  <p>TikTok video specs for 2026, from TikTok's own pages: record up to 10 minutes in the app, upload up to 60. Auction in-feed ads take a vertical 9:16 video at 540 by 960 pixels or more, up to 10 minutes and 500 MB. hubStudio publishes one clip of 3 seconds to 10 minutes to TikTok, a feature still in Beta.</p>

  <p>Reviewed October 8, 2026. Every number below comes from TikTok's Help Center, its Ads Manager help pages, or the template files those pages link, read that day. The consumer help center prints no update date, so its rows carry the read date. The ads pages print a month, and each row shows it.</p>

  <p>One absence matters before the tables. TikTok's help center publishes no aspect ratio, resolution, file size, format or bitrate for an ordinary post. Size guides that print one are quoting another source.</p>

