  <h3>What size should a TikTok video be?</h3>

  <p>TikTok's ads help asks for a vertical 9:16 video at 540 by 960 pixels or more, and its creative best practices recommend at least 720p. For ordinary posts, TikTok's help center prints no size at all. A 9:16 file that clears the ad floors, with text inside the template safe zone, is the safe build for both.</p>

  <h3>How long can a TikTok video be in 2026?</h3>

  <p>Up to 10 minutes when you record in the TikTok app and up to 60 minutes when you upload, per TikTok's help center on October 8, 2026. A sound picked first caps the length at the sound's length. Auction in-feed ads run up to 10 minutes, while reservation in-feed ads and TopView run 5 to 60 seconds.</p>

  <h3>What is the TikTok safe zone in pixels?</h3>

  <p>On TikTok's standard in-feed template, scaled to 1080 by 1920, keep text out of the top 240 pixels, the bottom 660 and 120 on each side, plus a 300-pixel right margin below the 840 mark. Anchor templates push the bottom up to 1,014 pixels with a four-line caption.</p>

  <h3>What are the TikTok in-feed ad specs?</h3>

